menu "DriveLink main"

    config DRIVELINK_STACK_LOG_PERIOD_S
        int "Task stack high-water log period (s)"
        default 30
        range 0 3600
        help
            While app_main idles, log the smallest free stack (high-water
            mark, in bytes) of each firmware task this often. 0 turns the
            log off. Used to size task stacks. Compiled out when
            DIAG_CONSOLE_LOG is off (no console text).

    config CORE_BOOT_SELFTEST
        bool "Core boot self-test (bench check only)"
        default n
        help
            A hardware check of the core's NVS persistence, for the bench
            only: never commit it on. After the core starts, main flips the
            system param control.rate_hz between 1000 and 500 and SAVEs it,
            so every boot after the first logs that it reloaded the value
            from NVS. It changes the control loop rate on every boot.

endmenu
